like Unicode 25B3 minor: -, like Unicode 002D augmented: +, like Unicode 002B diminished:"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"°, like Unicode 00B0 half-diminished: ø, like Unicode 00F8","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For the major-minor kind, only the minor symbol is used when use-symbols is yes. The major symbol is set using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the symbol attribute in the degree-value element. The corresponding degree-alter value will usually be 0 in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this case.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The text attribute describes how the kind should be spelled in a score. If use-symbols is yes, the value of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the text attribute follows the symbol. The stack-degrees attribute is yes if the degree elements should be","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"stacked above each other. The parentheses-degrees attribute is yes if all the degrees should be in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parentheses. The bracket-degrees attribute is yes if all the degrees should be in a bracket. If not specified,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"these values are implementation-specific. The alignment attributes are for the entire harmony-chord group of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which this kind element is a part.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The text attribute may use strings such as “13sus” that refer to both the kind and one or more degree","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements. In this case, the corresponding degree elements should have the print-object attribute set to “no”","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to keep redundant alterations from being displayed.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Kind indicates t